d":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008991377460006333,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":38.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":41.90859564164649,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.21264,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Roivant Sciences Ltd., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on the discovery, development, and commercialization of medicines and technologies. Its clinical product candidates include IMVT-1402, a fully human monoclonal antibody targeting FcRn in development across several IgG-mediated autoimmune indications; mosliciguat, an inhaled sGC activator in development for pulmonary hypertension associated with interstitial lung disease; neonatal fragment crystallizable receptor for the treatment of graves' disease, difficult-to-treat rheumatoid arthritis, sj\u00f6gren's disease, myasthenia gravis, chronic inflammatory demyelinating polyneuropathy, and cutaneous lupus erythematosus indications; batoclimab, a fully human monoclonal antibody for the treatment of thyroid eye disease; and brepocitinib, a potent small molecule inhibitor of TYK2 and JAK1 in development for the treatment of dermatomyositis, non-infectious uveitis, cutaneous sarcoidosis, and other immune-mediated diseases. The company's lead program consists of mosliciguat, an inhaled sGC activator for the treatment of pulmonary hypertension associated with interstitial lung disease and other cardiopulmonary diseases. In addition, the company offers delivery platforms comprising a lipid nanoparticle (LNP) platform and a ligand conjugate platform. Roivant Sciences Ltd. was founded in 2014 and is based in London, United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Matthew  Gline | CEO & Director | Age 41 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 721 people. Revenue per employee of $11K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 47%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $480K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 270\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Roivant Sciences Ltd. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $28.6B market cap on $8M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -47% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -219% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $759M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 4191% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 21% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 0/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 6235% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.12156166814551929},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.9% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $22.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 224% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(ROIV) Price Dynamics and Execution-Aware Positioning","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/ROIV_Price_Dynamics_and_Execution-Aware_Positioning_111326085401_1794578041.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794578041.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Roivant Sciences (NASDAQ:ROIV) Price Target Raised to $48.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/roivant-sciences-nasdaqroiv-price-target-raised-to-48-00.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794553290.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.765,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Roivant Sciences (ROIV) Could Be 312% Above Fair Value Following LISRAYA Launch And Trial Data","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-roiv/roivant-